# Netlify redirect rules. One per line: <source> <target> <status>
# https://docs.netlify.com/routing/redirects

# TestFlight public-beta shortcut.
# Apple's join URL is opaque (testflight.apple.com/join/<code>); this lets
# us share https://trymercurius.com/beta everywhere — Instagram, posters,
# QR codes — and keep the underlying TestFlight URL out of the public copy.
# 302 (temporary) because the join code rotates if the external-testing
# group is ever recreated; 301 would get aggressively cached and outlive
# the actual link.
# Netlify redirect matching is case-sensitive, so list the common-typed
# capitalizations explicitly (phones autocapitalize the first letter).
# /beta/ with a trailing slash is already handled by Netlify automatically.
/beta   https://testflight.apple.com/join/3ujBtDsa   302
/Beta   https://testflight.apple.com/join/3ujBtDsa   302
/BETA   https://testflight.apple.com/join/3ujBtDsa   302

# "Get the app" shortcut for posters, bios and the club site.
# Points at the App Store listing (flipped from TestFlight on 2026-10-24,
# while the TestFlight public link was closed). 302, not 301, so the target
# can change again without browsers holding on to the old one; all three
# capitalizations, same reasoning as /beta above.
/get    https://apps.apple.com/app/id6773192313   302
/Get    https://apps.apple.com/app/id6773192313   302
/GET    https://apps.apple.com/app/id6773192313   302

# Clean URLs for every page (the canonical URLs are the short form).
# 200 = rewrite, so the address bar keeps the short form and the existing
# .html links keep working too.
/features       /features.html       200
/modes          /modes.html          200
/how-it-works   /how-it-works.html   200
/audience       /audience.html       200
/trust          /trust.html          200
/support        /support.html        200
/privacy        /privacy.html        200
/terms          /terms.html          200
/ads            /ads.html            200

# In-app "Send feedback" (Settings → About) points here. Until the pilot's
# Google Form exists this lands on the support page (which carries the
# support@ address); swap the target for the form URL when it is created.
/feedback   /support.html   302
/Feedback   /support.html   302

# No rules for files that shouldn't be public: keep them out of this folder.
# Netlify publishes every file here and finds files whatever the case of the
# URL, while rules match it exactly, so a rule can't hide one (on the live
# site /rEaDmE.md served the old README and /bEta was a 404, though /beta
# redirects; no list of README rules covers every spelling). The site's docs
# are docs/marketing-site.md; tests/marketingNotFound.test.js fails on a file
# here that isn't part of the site.
